# draft holds no state, so there is very little to ignore.
#
# skills/draft/references/tools.md IS committed, even though `draft sync`
# generates it. A checkout should carry a working skill, and `draft check`
# already reports when it has drifted from the installed binaries -- which
# is information rather than a nuisance: a design planned against tools
# that have moved on is exactly what the drift check exists to catch.

# prove's crash journal. It exists only between a kill and the next run,
# which recovers from it and removes it.
.draft-prove-restore/

*.bak
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
